<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n23292" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">in-frendĕo</span></b> ,
		ēre, and <b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">in-frendo</span></b> , ĕre, v. n.,
			<div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b><i>to gnash</i>
			the teeth (<b>poet.</b> and postclass.): 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">dentibus infrendens gemitu,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Verg.
					A. 3, 664</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">ac simul infrendens,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Stat.
					Th. 5, 663</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">infrendite, inspumate,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Tert. Apol. 12</span></i>
			. —</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>II.</b>
			<i>To gnash the teeth at</i>, <i>threaten
				furiously;</i> with <i>dat.</i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">aliis infrendentem,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Stat.
					Th. 8, 580</span></i>
			.</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
